  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="2cba9f5d-8a29-47f5-8c43-8db679437249"><problem><para>
      <para>Mai and Jada are solving the equation \(2x^2−7x=15\) using the quadratic formula.</para>
      <para>Answer the following questions about the values of \(a\), \(b\), and \(c\) if this equation is written in standard form, \(ax^2+bx+c=0\).</para>
      <para>Enter the value of \(a\)?</para>
      </para></problem><solution><para>2</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is 2. The value of \(a=2\). </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
